The figure below shows a grid of $10$ squares in a row. Each square has a diagonal connecting its lower left vertex to its upper right vertex. A bug moves along the line segments from vertex to vertex, never traversing the same segment twice and never moving from right to left along a horizontal or diagonal segment. Let $N$ be the number of paths the bug can take from the lower left corner ($A$) to the upper right corner ($B$). One such path from $A$ to $B$ is shown by the thick line segments in the figure. Find $\sqrt{N}$.

[asy]
size(12cm);
draw((0, 0)--(0, 1));
for (int i = 0; i <= 9; i += 1)
{
draw((i, 1)--(i + 1, 1)--(i + 1, 0)--(i, 0)--(i + 1, 1));
}
draw((0, 0)--(0, 1)--(2, 1)--(2, 0)--(3, 1)--(3, 0)--(4, 1)--(4, 0)--(5, 0)--(5, 1)--(6, 1)--(6, 0)--(7, 1)--(8, 1)--(8, 0)--(10, 0)--(10, 1), red + linewidth(2));
label("$A$", (0, 0), dir(180));
label("$B$", (10, 1), dir(0));
[/asy]

Define the sequences $(a_n),(b_n)$ by
\begin{align*}
& a_n, b_n > 0, \forall n\in\mathbb{N_+} \\ 
& a_{n+1} = a_n - \frac{1}{1+\sum_{i=1}^n\frac{1}{a_i}} \\ 
& b_{n+1} = b_n + \frac{1}{1+\sum_{i=1}^n\frac{1}{b_i}}
\end{align*}
1) If $a_{100}b_{100} = a_{101}b_{101}$, find the value of $a_1-b_1$;
2) If $a_{100} = b_{99}$, determine which is larger between $a_{100}+b_{100}$ and $a_{101}+b_{101}$.

